# Workbooks Documentation

facet app

The docs site for Workbooks, authored as a workbook — prose narrates, `do … end`
blocks run. This `index.work` is the **composition root**: it names the site and
the ordered sections/pages the sidebar shows. The nexus serves the tree as a
navigable site; the look comes from `design.work` (our brand sheet), never from the
runtime — the same unopinionated image anyone deploys.

app :docs do
  title "Workbooks"            # the look lives in design.work — the runtime is unopinionated plumbing

  section "Preface" do
    page "preface/literate-programming"
    page "preface/why-webassembly"
  end

  section "Introduction" do
    page "introduction/what-is-a-workbook"
    page "introduction/what-is-a-work-file"
    page "introduction/what-is-the-nexus"
    page "introduction/what-is-the-work-cli"
    page "introduction/what-is-workbooks-cloud"
  end

  section "Architecture" do
    page "architecture/one-frontend-many-targets"
    page "architecture/runtime-connect-rcp"
    page "architecture/build-tier-and-compile-cache"
  end

  section "The .work language" do
    page "language/anatomy"
    page "language/block-grammar"
    page "language/prose-and-refs"
    page "language/hash-notes"
    page "language/declarations"
    page "language/placement-and-languages"
    page "language/kinds-reference"
    page "language/concurrency-and-workers"
    page "language/elixir-in-markdown"
  end

  section "Capabilities & sandboxing" do
    page "capabilities/sandboxing-and-the-dock"
    page "capabilities/grants-and-capabilities"
    page "capabilities/the-three-walls"
  end

  section "Data & persistence" do
    page "data/resources-and-the-store"
  end

  section "Serving & routing" do
    page "serving/routes-and-pages"
    page "serving/site-mode-and-llms-txt"
  end

  section "Running & deploying" do
    page "deploy/running-the-nexus"
    page "deploy/deploy-local-and-cloud"
    page "deploy/deploy-as-index-tree"
    page "deploy/secrets-and-config"
    page "deploy/workbooks-cloud"
  end

  section "Agents & tooling" do
    page "tooling/get-started-with-your-cli-agent"
    page "tooling/authoring-an-agent"
    page "tooling/toolkits"
  end

  section "Examples" do
    page "examples/coding-agent"
    page "examples/autonomous-research"
    page "examples/agents-at-scale"
  end

  section "Blog" do
    page "blog/why-we-author-docs-as-a-workbook"
    page "blog/the-nexus-serves-many-sites"
  end
end

# ── Workspace composition: docs pages are CONTENT of the docs site, not workspace surfaces. These three
# pages embed example `resource` code to teach declarations, which auto-discovery mis-reads as data
# stores — hide them from the Studio sidebar (they still serve as docs pages on the site).
workspace do
  hide "language/declarations.work"
  hide "data/resources-and-the-store.work"
  hide "skills/authoring_work_files/references/declarations.work"
end
